      "id": "bbc-2026-11-24-world-cup-drove-profits-surge-says-marston-s",
      "title": "World Cup drove profits surge, says Marston's",
      "summary": "The company says an \"excellent World Cup\" helped drive strong trading as annual profits rose by 18%.",
      "body": "Pub company Marston's has said an \"excellent World Cup\" helped drive stronger trading as annual profits rose by nearly a fifth, despite reporting a dip in sales. The Wolverhampton-based firm, which operates more than 1,300 pubs across the UK, reported underlying pre-tax profits of £85.4m for the year to 26 September, up 18.4% from a year earlier.The company said trading was improved by new-look pubs, strong trade during this summer's football World Cup, and a partnership with Jeremy Clarkson's Hawkstone drinks brand. \"For the third year running, profit is significantly up, cash flow is strong and margins have improved,\" said chief executive Justin Platt. The pub chain also said bookings for Christmas events were 9% ahead of the same point last year.Marston's has invested heavily in refurbishing pubs into new formats, including its sports-focused \"Grandstand\" venues.It plans at least 100 more conversions in the new financial year, in a bid to accelerate sales growth further.One of the busiest locals during the World Cup was The New Spires in Coventry, which reopened in March following a £400,000 makeover.",
      "source": "BBC",
      "category": "business",
      "tags": [],
      "author": null,
      "publishedAt": "2026-11-24T13:03:20.000Z",
