      "id": "hackernews-2026-11-24-who-in-washington-owns-and-trades-nvidia-stock",
      "title": "Who in Washington owns and trades Nvidia stock",
      "summary": "Article URL: https://www.kadoa.com/congress/insights/trump-nvidia\nComments URL: https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50626861\nPoints: 250\n# Comments: 127",
      "body": "Every disclosed Nvidia stock trade by Trump and 37 members of Congress, around Jensen Huang's resignation and reinstatement.Nvidia fell 48% from its October high to 20 November, through Huang's resignation and quarterly results. It rose 33% on 23 November, when the board reinstated him, citing input from senior levels of the US government (NBC News).Trump's trades in Nvidia stock in 202628 purchases ($5.1M to $16.7M) and 15 sales ($4.4M to $12M), plotted on Nvidia's daily close. His latest report, released 19 Nov 2026, runs to 24 September.▲ Purchase▼ SaleLarger: higher valueHuang outMay not be reported yetMembers of Congress who traded Nvidia stock since January 2025192 trades by 37 members, largest totals first. The latest disclosed trade is from 28 October. Periodic transaction reports only.▲ Purchase▼ SaleValue≤ $15K≤ $250K> $250KHuang outMay not be reported yetAbout the dataHoldings: Trump's annual report values his Nvidia stock at $12.5M to $58M on 31 December 2025, or 67,000 to 311,000 shares at that day's close.If he still held them, he lost $0.5 million to $2.2 million from 11 to 23 November. We can't tell whether he did: his 2026 trades are reported in ranges too wide to net.His accounts are run by independent managers, according to the Trump Organization (AP). The reports don't show who decided a trade.Trades can be reported up to 45 days late, so November's will appear by early January. We'll update the page then.Congress: periodic transaction reports only, including family accounts. Trades in annual or candidate reports, like those NOTUS found for Eric Swalwell and Ritchie Torres, aren't included.",
