      "id": "bbc-2026-11-23-raya-to-miss-dortmund-game-but-injury-not-serious",
      "title": "Raya to miss Dortmund game but injury 'not serious'",
      "summary": "Arsenal goalkeeper David Raya will miss Tuesday's Champions League game against Borussia Dortmund but his shoulder injury will not require an operation.",
      "body": "Arsenal goalkeeper David Raya's shoulder injury \"doesn't look too serious\", but he will miss Tuesday's Champions League against Borussia Dortmund, says Mikel Arteta.Raya was helped off the pitch in the 70th minute of Arsenal's 2-2 draw at Newcastle on Saturday.He hurt his left shoulder while claiming a cross and making contact with Newcastle forward William Osula. \"We need some more tests [on Tuesday] but it is quite encouraging,\" said Gunners boss Arteta.\"He is not fit [to face Dortmund] but it doesn't look too serious.\" Arteta said that while the incident looked pretty innocuous the pain his keeper was in made him fear it was a serious injury.\"With the pain that he was showing immediately after the action we were all quite worried but it seems to be better than what we expected,\" said Arteta.\"When you look at the action it doesn't seem to be much but the extent of the pain that he had and how he was struggling, it was quite worrying.\"We expected something much worse because he could almost not handle the amount of pain he had in that moment.\"The first tests that we have done have shown something that is much more encouraging. He does not need to have surgery which was the worry as that would rule him out for months so let's see.\"",
      "source": "BBC",
      "category": "world",
      "tags": [],
      "author": null,
      "publishedAt": "2026-11-23T15:23:09.000Z",
      "imageUrl": "https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/ace/branded_sport/1200/cpsprodpb/65dc/live/03482e80-e753-11f1-88dc-f746e0cde621.jpg",
