      "id": "theverge-2026-11-23-amazon-is-taking-orders-for-the-moto-tag-3-before-it-s-even-",
      "title": "Amazon is taking orders for the Moto Tag 3 before it’s even been announced",
      "summary": "Are these actually new, or just fresh color variants of the Moto Tag 2? | Image: Evan Blass\t\n\nMotorola's unannounced Moto Tag 3 has been listed for sale online, just five months after the Moto Tag 2 went on sale in the US, and before any official announcement of a follow-up. The listing on Amazon UK was spotted by X user @matteventu, and shows the tracker in a \"Pantone Lucent White\" color option, ",
      "body": "Motorola’s unannounced Moto Tag 3 has been listed for sale online, just five months after the Moto Tag 2 went on sale in the US, and before any official announcement of a follow-up. The listing on Amazon UK was spotted by X user @matteventu, and shows the tracker in a “Pantone Lucent White” color option, with a price of £24.96 (about $33) and a 1-4 month shipping estimate.\nA second image shared by leaker Evan Blass also shows a vibrant purple version of the new tracking tag, which is described as “Pantone Indigo Blue” on a separate Amazon Italy listing. Both are new color options, with the Moto Tag 2 only currently available in orange or a grey-ish beige. While the Moto Tag 3 name suggests this is a follow-up to the Moto Tag 2, there don’t appear to be any major hardware differences between the two trackers.\nBoth use a replaceable CR2032 battery, claim to provide more than 500 days of battery life, and support UWB in Android Find Hub, among other similarities. The XT2561-1 model number seen on the back of the Moto Tag 3 images also matches that of the Moto Tag 2. That could mean that the Moto Tag 3 name is an error and these are just new color options for the Tag 2.\nWe’ve asked Motorola for clarification and will update if we hear back.",
      "source": "The Verge",
      "category": "tech",
      "tags": [
        "Android",
        "Google",
        "Motorola",
        "News",
        "Tech"
      ],
      "author": "Jess Weatherbed",
      "publishedAt": "2026-11-23T13:09:32.000Z",
