      "id": "bbc-2026-11-23-south-east-water-reports-loss-after-supply-issues",
      "title": "South East Water reports loss after supply issues",
      "summary": "South East Water records a pre-tax loss of £22.9m in the six months to 30 September.",
      "body": "In October, it was forced to ask shareholders for £50m after warning earlier in the year that it required additional funding in order to stay afloat. The company said there were \"early signs of improvement\" following changes to its leadership team and plans for a \"significant transformation\" of the business.Earlier this year, John Halsall was appointed chief executive after former chief executive David Hinton and chair Chris Train stepped down.The departures followed criticism from MPs who said they had \"no confidence\" in the company's leadership after a review of repeated supply outages.Richard Morse is due to become chair of the company on 3 December, succeeding interim chair Lisa Clement.South East Water said the initial signs were \"encouraging\", although it warned improvements would take time to become fully visible to customers.A spokesperson for the company said: \"We know that customers will not judge us on the number of initiatives we launch or the promises we make.\"They will judge us on whether their water supply is more reliable, whether we communicate better and whether we provide the right support when they need it – we look forward to providing the evidence in future results.\"Follow BBC Kent on Facebook, external,  X, external, and on Instagram, external and listen to BBC Radio Kent on Sounds. Send your story ideas to southeasttoday@bbc.co.uk, external or WhatsApp us on 08081 002250.",
