      "id": "bbc-2026-11-23-manchester-s-co-op-live-evacuated-after-unknown-substance-le",
      "title": "Manchester's Co-op Live evacuated after 'unknown substance' let off in crowd",
      "summary": "One person was taken to hospital after a major incident was declared during a performance by US rapper Don Toliver.",
      "body": "Thousands of people were evacuated from a concert in Manchester on Sunday night after an \"unknown substance\" was released into the crowd, police said.The incident happened towards the end of US rapper Don Toliver's show at the Co-op Live arena at about 22:00.The North West Ambulance Service said one person was taken to hospital for further assessment while more than 50 people were assessed for \"eye and respiratory symptoms\".Greater Manchester Police (GMP) said a major incident was declared after reports of people suffering from the effects of an unknown substance, which police initially believed to be tear gas.Footage on social media showed emergency services converge on the arena, while some concertgoers were seen coughing as they streamed out of the venue.  In a statement early on Monday, GMP said more than 12,000 people had been safely evacuated, with several people assessed for side effects.\"Our priority was to ensure the safety of every person that was attending the concert,\" GMP Assistant Chief Constable Steph Parker said.\"Several people were treated on site, and one has been taken to hospital at this time. Anyone who has left the event and since become unwell is advised to attend their local hospital.\"We understand the concern that this incident will have raised – particularly those with loved ones at the venue last night – and we'd like to thank everyone for their patience as we dealt with it.\"",
