      "id": "hackernews-2026-11-22-0rwx-a-simple-model-of-ai-usage-inspired-by-unix-permissions",
      "title": "0rwx – A simple model of AI usage, inspired by Unix permissions",
      "summary": "Article URL: https://0rwx.com/\nComments URL: https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50605445\nPoints: 33\n# Comments: 6",
      "body": "We need new language to talk about large language models. 0rwx is my attempt.\nA labelling system is vital for domain experts to talk about AI in a clear way.\nThe difference between the 4 levels is not necessarily about what TOOL you use, but your ability to scrutinise the generated work.\nI have employed this simple framework to discuss my and others' work with less judgement and confusion,\nand I hope the 0rwx framework makes it just a little easier for you too. They are:\nAI can't read or write to your work\nYOU can no longer read your work\nYou are welcome to use these logos, which I release into the public domain. Find more options at the repo!",
