      "title": "What's next after no deal at COP31 climate talks?",
      "summary": "The talks have been the longest-running in the summit's history, with negotiations breaking down two days after they had been due to end.",
      "body": "The COP31 climate summit in Turkey has officially come to an end after countries failed to come to a consensus on a new deal.The European Union and some other countries rejected a fourth draft agreement over its failure to mention a need to phase out fossil fuels, the largest driver of global climate change.An EU representative accuses some oil states of hijacking talks, as Russia defends opposing the inclusion of such a commitment and levels direct criticism at the EU in its speech.The talks have been the longest-running in the summit's history, with negotiations breaking down two days after they had been due to end.BBC climate and science reporter Esme Stallard reports from Antalya, in Turkey.",
