      "id": "bbc-2026-11-22-russell-brand-s-wife-says-she-ll-honour-prison-rules-after-m",
      "title": "Russell Brand's wife says she'll honour prison rules after message row",
      "summary": "The wife of the disgraced comedian says she will stick to the \"parameters\", after reading out a message from her inmate husband.",
      "body": "The wife of disgraced comedian Russell Brand says she will \"honour\" the rules of his prison, a week after she read a message from her husband proclaiming his innocence.Laura Brand, 39, drew criticism from ministers after reading out the message from inside HMP Littlehey last week, prompting the government to seek to have the episode removed from social media platforms.She said on Sunday that she would continue to defend her family and herself over her portrayal in the media during the couple's weekly podcast, which she now presents alone.Russell Brand, 51, is currently serving a 10-and-half-year prison sentence after being convicted of rape and three counts of sexual assault.\"Last week's episode drew a considerable amount of attention,\" Laura Brand said during this week's episode of Sunday Service. \"Now that I understand the parameters set by the brilliant and professional staff at HMP Littlehey, I will absolutely honour that.\"In the relayed message last week, Russell Brand had said he was \"not guilty of the offences I have been jailed for\".Laura Brand said she had spoken to him at the Cambridgeshire prison and said he was \"OK\".Russell Brand was found guilty of raping a woman at his home in 2009, as well as three counts of sexual assault against three other women.Further allegations have since been reported about him and some have called for consent laws to be revised.His conviction has renewed conversation about safeguarding in the media industry, and whether some celebrities are still able to use their fame to prey on women and then silence them.Ministers have pointed out that inmates are prohibited from making statements that are likely to cause their victims distress and have said Brand's message was being investigated.A woman who alleges she was raped by Brand when she was 16, but who was not among the women whose accusations led to his conviction, said his prison message was \"upsetting\" and \"really shocking\".The government attempted to have the podcast removed from YouTube, but this was refused by its owner Google. Prime Minister Andy Burnham urged social media companies to \"show some decency and take these videos down\".On Sunday, Laura Brand also said that Sunday Service would be a place where she would \"continue to be proud to be a wife, a mother and a woman defending her family at a time when the media's image of what kind of a woman I am is under so much scrutiny\". She expressed feeling a mixture of \"grief\", \"absence\", \"desolation\" and \"loneliness\" since her husband's imprisonment.",
      "source": "BBC",
      "category": "world",
      "tags": [],
      "author": null,
      "publishedAt": "2026-11-22T16:51:57.000Z",
      "imageUrl": "https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/ace/branded_news/1200/cpsprodpb/7ba9/live/b922d470-e691-11f1-936e-1fd1d31671db.jpg",
