      "id": "theverge-2026-11-22-how-tamagotchis-got-us-hooked-on-digital-pets",
      "title": "How Tamagotchis got us hooked on digital pets",
      "summary": "If you were are a kid in the late 1990s, there's a near-100 percent chance you either had a Tamagotchi or knew someone who did. The tiny digital pets came out of nowhere and became an overnight sensation, as millions of kids signed up to parent a crying, hungry, constantly dirty creature. Until they went to school, anyway, at which point their parents were given some new responsibilities they neit",
      "body": "If you were are a kid in the late 1990s, there’s a near-100 percent chance you either had a Tamagotchi or knew someone who did. The tiny digital pets came out of nowhere and became an overnight sensation, as millions of kids signed up to parent a crying, hungry, constantly dirty creature. Until they went to school, anyway, at which point their parents were given some new responsibilities they neither asked for nor wanted.\nOn this episode of Version History, we dig deep into the story of the Tamagotchi. That story has its 30th anniversary this week, even though the real craze only lasted a few years. David Pierce is joined by The Verge’s Mia Sato and Victoria Song to discuss the origins of the Tamagotchi, the product’s many iterations, its incredible engagement tactics, and whether any of us could tolerate the Tama experience three decades later. (We… could not.)\nThis is the second episode of the sixth season of Version History, all about tech for your pets — and tech that is pets. Last week we fell back in love with the Sony Aibo, and there’s lots more to come this season. f you want to be sure not to miss anything, there are a few ways to subscribe:\n* The Version History podcast feed\n* The Version History YouTube channel\n* Our TikTok and Instagram accounts\nIf you’re a Verge subscriber, you can also get access to Version History (and all our other podcasts) with no ads. All you have to do is visit your account settings.\nIf you want to know more about the Tamagotchi, here are some links to get you started:\n* From The New York Times in 1997: The Tamagotchi: Toy Life-Form Invades the U.S.\n* From Smithsonian: A Brief History of Tamagotchi\n* From RetroDodo: The CRAZY History Of Tamagotchi\n* From BBC World Service: Witness History, Tamagotchi is born\n* The AI Tamagotchis are coming",
      "source": "The Verge",
      "category": "tech",
      "tags": [
        "Gadgets",
        "Podcasts",
        "Tech",
        "Version History"
      ],
      "author": "David Pierce",
      "publishedAt": "2026-11-22T13:15:27.000Z",
      "imageUrl": "https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2026/11/VRH_Tamagotchi_Site.jpg?quality=90&strip=all&crop=0%2C10.732984293194%2C100%2C78.534031413613&w=1200",
