      "id": "bbc-2026-11-22-mp-criticises-guernsey-and-jersey-company-ownership-register",
      "title": "MP criticises Guernsey and Jersey company ownership register plans",
      "summary": "Sir Andrew Mitchell says access should be easier for people tackling financial crime.",
      "body": "Plans to improve transparency over company ownership in Guernsey and Jersey have come under criticism from a Westminster MP, who says they \"do not go nearly far enough\".The comments come after Guernsey, external and Jersey, external set out plans to allow approved applicants access to information about who owns or controls companies when investigating suspected financial crime.Sir Andrew Mitchell, who has campaigned for greater scrutiny of company ownership, said there were \"immediate indications\" the proposals would fall short.He said limits on access to the information could mean \"national security threats may remain entirely invisible to investigators\".The plans follow a joint commitment made by Guernsey, Jersey and the Isle of Man in December 2023 to increase transparency around company ownership and help tackle money laundering, terrorist financing and other financial crime.Currently, information about who ultimately owns or controls companies is generally only available to law enforcement agencies, regulators and certain regulated businesses carrying out anti-money laundering checks.The new proposals would allow journalists, academics and other applicants with a legitimate interest to apply for access.",
      "source": "BBC",
      "category": "business",
      "tags": [],
      "author": null,
      "publishedAt": "2026-11-22T07:22:05.000Z",
