      "id": "hackernews-2026-11-22-show-hn-the-riemann-proof-handbook",
      "title": "Show HN: The Riemann Proof Handbook",
      "summary": "Article URL: https://github.com/tamnd/riemann-handbook\nComments URL: https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50596664\nPoints: 71\n# Comments: 42",
      "body": "A book, in PDF and EPUB, that writes the Lean proof of the Riemann Hypothesis in tamnd/riemann-lean as mathematics: definitions, theorems, lemmas and their proofs, in words.\nThe claim is not checked. Nobody has built the Lean project in full yet, and no person has checked the written statements against the Lean code. This book explains the Lean code. It is not a separate check of the mathematics. See What is checked.\nGuide: how to read, the status of the claim, notation, the named results, the index of Lean names\nBackground: the mathematics that the proof uses, in 17 chapters\nthe Learn pages of tamnd/riemann\nThe proof: the top of the proof, its chapters and steps\nthe written proof of tamnd/riemann\nThe Lean development, one branch or one Lean folder in each volume\ncontent/dev/, written for this book\nThe books are in the releases.\nThe plan of the development volumes\nEach declaration of the proof is inside the dominated subtree of exactly one other declaration (its immediate dominator, in the graph of uses from riemannHypothesis). The ledger gives an entry to each declaration whose dominated subtree is large, in tiers: 1,000 or more declarations (591 entries), 300 or more (1,927), 100 or more (5,764). It assigns each entry to a volume by its branch of the proof or by its Lean folder, and to a chapter by its Lean folder. In a chapter, the entries come from the top of the proof down.\npython -m rhb ledger --records /path/to/records --min 1000 --write\nledger/coverage.md has the numbers. prompts/entry.md is the brief for the writers of entries.\nYou need Python 3.11 or later, pandoc 3.8 or later and Tectonic. Put tamnd/riemann and tamnd/riemann-lean next to this repository.\npython -m rhb build --volume 0,1,2 --formats pdf,epub\nThe books go to build/. The pipeline is that of The Handbook of Algorithms: Markdown, then pandoc with filters/rhb.lua, then LaTeX with tex/handbook.sty, then Tectonic. The EPUB is EPUB 3 with MathML.\nThe text is licensed under CC BY 4.0, as the text of tamnd/riemann. The builder is licensed under the MIT licence.\nPlease report errors at issues.",
      "source": "Hacker News",
      "category": "tech",
      "tags": [],
      "author": "tamnd",
      "publishedAt": "2026-11-22T05:46:30.000Z",
