      "id": "hackernews-2026-11-21-tasklet-yc-p26-is-hiring-product-and-agent-infra-engineers",
      "title": "Tasklet (YC P26) Is Hiring Product and Agent Infra Engineers",
      "summary": "Article URL: https://tasklet.ai/careers\nComments URL: https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50593679\nPoints: 0\n# Comments: 0",
      "body": "Careers at TaskletBuild the AI workforce.AI is moving from answering questions to owning work. Join a small team in San Francisco building AI employees that companies can trust with real responsibilities, around the clock.All positions are full-time and in-person in our San Francisco office.Head of Design EngineeringDefine and build how people hire, onboard, and work alongside AI employees.View role →Software Engineer — PlatformBuild the foundations that let a company connect its tools, share AI employees, and stay in control.View role →Software Engineer — AI InfraTurn frontier models, parallel workers, and cloud computers into dependable AI employees.View role →Software Engineer — ProductMake delegating real work to AI employees feel simple, natural, and trustworthy.View role →Customer Success EngineerHelp businesses put AI employees to work—and use what you learn to make the product better.View role →Apply by sending a videoShow us who you are.To apply, email our CEO Andrew (andrew@tasklet.ai) with a video introduction of yourself. Include your resume & any relevant links so we can learn more about you.Your video must be 5 minutes or less and include the following:Who you are & why you want to join TaskletA confirmation that you are able to work full-time, in-person in SF (including any required work authorizations - we are not sponsoring new visas at this time)A demo of the most impressive thing you've made recently that’s relevant to the role you’re applying for. Make sure to show what you made, not just tell us.About TaskletBetter models are only the beginning.We believe every company will have AI employees. Not another chatbot to prompt or a workflow to babysit, but teammates with real responsibilities: closing the books, keeping a sales pipeline moving, helping customers, and following through on the work between messages. Tasklet is building the product that makes those employees possible.Our vision is a team of virtual teammates that learn your business, collaborate with your people, and follow through around the clock. Customers already build custom agents, connect their business tools, and work with them in Tasklet, Slack, email, and text. We’re making it easier for an entire company to work with those agents—and for the people responsible to understand and control what they do.The hard part is everything between a capable model and a colleague you can depend on. We combine models from multiple labs, swarms of parallel workers, cloud computers, and connections to business systems in one agent harness. Then we make that power understandable: what an agent owns, what it did, when it needs help, and what it is allowed to do next.The AI labs are racing to build better models. We’re racing to turn that intelligence into a workforce businesses can actually rely on. We can use the best technology from any lab and focus our entire company on that problem. This is a chance to help define a new category of software—not add one more feature to the old one.A small team with a proven track record.Our team of 14 is based in San Francisco and is led by founders Andrew Lee (formerly founded Firebase & sold it to Google) and Jonny Dimond and includes Will Chambers, Hiranya Jayathilaka, Michael Lehenbauer, Michael Latman, Parker Chun, Christiana Stubblefield, Tyler Rockwood, Mark Robinson, Geoff Hamilton, Austin Haag, Brennan Murphy, and Dan Sundberg.We’ve built the kinds of systems this moment demands: agent systems, cloud infrastructure, and productivity tools. That experience comes from building Shortwave, Firebase, and critical infrastructure at Google, Amazon, OpenAI, Salesforce, and elsewhere. Here, you’ll work directly with the people who built them—and own a meaningful piece of what comes next.We run the company on our own AI employees. They handle real work in recruiting, support, and operations, and engineers direct parallel agents every day. If work can be delegated to an agent, we delegate it.CultureA high-performance, results-focused culture.Tasklet is a fast-paced, engineering-driven, results-oriented company. We aim to build a truly world-class team & an amazing work environment. These are the values we aspire to:Understand our users & solve their A+ problemsYou focus on the problems that really matter — not the ones you already know how to solve. You take responsibility for delivering experiences that our users love — end-to-end. This requires a deep understanding of our users, their workflows, and how AI agents can transform them.Relentlessly pursue a vision for excellence, but ship todayIn the world of AI agents, things change rapidly, and we intend to set the pace. You iterate with extreme urgency, shipping improvements daily that compound into transformative capabilities over time. You aim high, know where you're going, and don't stop until it's amazing.LeadYou accomplish far more through teamwork than you could individually. You enable teamwork by being a leader, and you lead by doing, not just by talking.Take initiativeYou act like an owner and make great things happen without being asked. You try to be the change you want to see in the world. You believe nothing is someone else's problem.Be honest & truth seekingYou’re committed to finding & communicating the truth. You follow evidence, not your ego. You speak your mind and let others speak theirs.Deliver business resultsYou know that results — not effort — are what counts, and you take responsibility for our hardest & most important work: figuring out what needs to be done to get the right results. You own the results you produce, including your failures.$20,000 referral bonusDo you know someone who's a great fit for any of our roles? Refer them to us and we will pay you $20k if we hire them. Simply have them apply and mention in their application that you referred them.Some eligibility restrictions apply:You must be a US residentYou must be the first person to refer someone to us (and we must not already be in contact with them)The candidate must start work within 3 months of your referralPayment will be made after their start dateEligibility decisions are made at our sole discretion",
