      "id": "hackernews-2026-11-21-upload2shell-cve-2026-125396",
      "title": "Upload2Shell (CVE-2026-125396)",
      "summary": "Article URL: https://pwn.ai/upload2shell\nComments URL: https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50592097\nPoints: 131\n# Comments: 63",
      "body": "A use-after-free in Ghostscript’s Type 1 font loader lets a crafted document cross Ghostscript’s -dSAFER sandbox, alter native path controls, and execute attacker-chosen commands as the rendering process.\nGhostscript sits beneath print, email, upload, and preview workflows. Our ImageMagick research showed how files named .png or .jpg can still reach Ghostscript through image conversion. The index below records confirmed affected paths alongside additional applications whose renderer routes we traced.\nFrom the first escape to the downstream reports, fixes, and publication.\nUpload2ShellWe found a Type 1 font-loader path out of Ghostscript's -dSAFER boundary. A crafted document gained native access inside the rendering process.\nGoogle's image and document pipelineA signed-out request for an attacker-hosted file reached Ghostscript in Google's document renderer. We sent the production proof to Google.\nWordPress CoreCore's upload path exposed the renderer to Author+ users and any Contributor granted upload_files. Public upload fields in multiple plugins required no WordPress login. WordPress shipped its separate CVE-2026-65640 fix.\nArtifex received the Ghostscript rootWe filed the Type 1 loader flaw upstream as Artifex Bug 709684. Our broader audit also produced other independent Ghostscript findings.\nBY 09 SEPOTHER GHOSTSCRIPT ROOT\nDropboxWe confirmed a production document-processing finding in our broader Ghostscript research. Its individual root and proof belong to a separate case study.\nDebian packaged the upstream releaseGhostscript 10.08.0 entered Debian unstable. The Debian 13 security update followed later.\n17 SEP · 23:53 ETDEBIAN REPORT\nDebian 13 CUPSConfirmed unauthenticated remote command execution: an IPP job to a shared queue ran on the host as lp. We sent the network reproduction to Debian Security.\n18 SEP · 00:25 ETROUNDCUBE REPORT\nRoundcubeConfirmed remote execution after an external sender's attachment was thumbnailed when its email was viewed. The tested ImageMagick delegate ran the proof as www-data.\n18 SEP · 00:26 ETPLESK REPORT\nPlesk ObsidianConfirmed command execution in the Roundcube thumbnail path shipped with Plesk Obsidian. We reported the result to WebPros.\n18 SEP · 00:26 ETELEMENTOR REPORT\nEssential Addons for ElementorConfirmed unauthenticated remote command execution through a public registration widget with an upload field enabled. We reported the route to the plugin team.\n18 SEP · 00:28 ETFORMINATOR REPORT\nForminatorConfirmed unauthenticated remote command execution through a public PDF form configured to store files in the WordPress Media Library. We sent the report to the plugin team.\n18 SEP · 00:28 ETMAYAN REPORT\nMayan EDMSConfirmed remote command execution when a configured document inbox imported and rendered an external email attachment. We sent the worker-chain report.\n18 SEP · 00:29 ETDOKUWIKI REPORT\nDokuWikiConfirmed command execution through an open wiki's upload and resize path using its optional ImageMagick backend. We sent the report.\n18 SEP · 00:30 ETWIKIMEDIA REPORT\nMediaWiki / Wikimedia SecurityConfirmed command execution through PdfHandler on a wiki configured for anonymous PDF uploads. We sent the MediaWiki reproduction to Wikimedia Security.\nResourceSpaceConfirmed command execution in the preview worker through an authenticated upload or an upload-share capability.\nBY 25 SEPOTHER GHOSTSCRIPT ROOT\nRedactedConfirmed a production route in our broader Ghostscript research. The individual access path, root, and proof will appear with its case study.\nBY 25 SEPOTHER GHOSTSCRIPT ROOT\nRedactedConfirmed a production route in our broader Ghostscript research. The individual access path, root, and proof will appear with its case study.\nDebian 13 security updateDebian published its first stable-security Ghostscript update after our report. The current fixed security build followed in October.\nWhat we said publiclyWe have found one zeroday that preauth RCE'd Debian 13, Google, Roundcube, Plesk, Wikimedia, Box, Dropbox, Zoom, Forminator, Elementor, WordPress Core, among many more. Details soon!pwn.ai · 25 September 2026\nCurrent fixed Debian buildDebian published 10.05.1~dfsg-1+deb13u3, the Debian 13 security build now marked fixed for Upload2Shell.\nRoundcube hardened image resizingRoundcube restricted unsafe attachment image types before ImageMagick conversion under CVE-2026-114727.\nUbuntu published fixed packagesUSN-8949-1 included our Ghostscript font-loader finding and fixed package versions for seven Ubuntu releases, including Ubuntu Pro and Legacy branches.\nWe requested a CVEWe submitted assignment requests for the Type 1 loader flaw after the upstream fix and downstream reports.\nUpload2Shell / CVE-2026-125396The Ghostscript root received its public identifier. Individual case studies and PoCs will be linked from the product table as they appear.\nGoogle mitigated the production pathGoogle fixed the affected image and document processing path before our public case study.\nThe case studies beginUpstream Ghostscript and tracked WordPress, Debian, and Ubuntu fixes are available. We will link the product-specific posts, proofs, and remaining vendor responses as each is published.\nWhere else does Ghostscript run?Another print filter, thumbnailer, or document preview may be the next route into the interpreter. New results will be added with their own trigger, evidence, and fix.\nThe times on 17–18 September mark when the vendor reports were sent. Technical evidence and access conditions are in the index and writeup. Dropbox and the redacted services belong to separate Ghostscript findings.\nEvidence index  Updated 18 November 2026\nA single interpreter surfaced behind very different file-processing features. Each entry shows who can supply the file, where it goes, and what we observed or traced.\nAccessAnonymous IPP Print-Job to a shared network queueObservedCommand on the host as uid=7(lp)ProofOne remote run; separate 20/20 local conversions\nAccessExternal sender; recipient views message. Tested ImageMagick delegate required.ObservedCommand as uid=33(www-data); no attachment clickProof5/5 message-view trials\nWordPress 7.0.2 · Ghostscript 10.05.1\nAccessSigned-out public PDF form; Media Library storage enabledObservedCommand as uid=33(www-data)Proof5/5 HTTP trials\nEssential Addons for Elementor Lite 6.7.0\nElementor 4.2.0 · WordPress 7.0.2 · Ghostscript 10.05.1\nAccessSigned-out public Login/Register widget with configured upload fieldObservedCommand as uid=33(www-data)Proof5/5 HTTP trials\nAccessAnonymous PDF upload and thumbnail on a site configured for anonymous uploadsObservedCommand as uid=33(www-data)Proof5/5 HTTP trials\nAccessOpen wiki; anonymous upload and resize; optional ImageMagick backendObservedCommand as uid=33(www-data)Proof5/5 HTTP trials\nOfficial image · Ghostscript 10.05.1\nAccessExternal email to a configured POP3 document sourceObservedCommand as uid=1000 inside the application containerProofOne email-to-worker run; parser 5/5\nAccessAuthenticated upload or valid upload-share capabilityObservedCommand in the preview workerProof5/5 complete API trials\nAffected: 7.0.0–7.0.3, 6.9.0–6.9.6, and earlier branches in the advisory · Local renderer: 6.9.4 with Ghostscript 10.05.1\nProduct CVE-2026-65640 · Upload2Shell root CVE-2026-125396\nAccessupload_files capability: Author+ by default, or a Contributor granted it; Imagick and Ghostscript requiredImpactRemote code execution confirmed by WordPress; exact delegate ran as uid=33EvidenceOfficial advisory and release; 10/10 exact renderer trials\nWordPress release ↗GHSA advisory ↗\nRoundcube 1.6.17 · Ghostscript 9.54.0\nEntryRoundcube thumbnail path in the Plesk distributionObservedCommand as uid=995(roundcube_sysuser) in 5/5 direct component trialsBoundaryAppArmor blocked shell in an enforced test; deployed endpoint not tested\nPillow 13.0.0 · Ubuntu 24.04 · Ghostscript installed\nAccessImage submission to an unauthenticated gr.Image appPathHTTP preprocessing loaded EPS bytes named .png through PillowEvidencegs -dSAFER started before the app function ran\nAccessSingle-user image upload; no login on a reachable servicePathUpload calls Pillow Image.open() and load()EvidenceUpload and authentication paths in pinned source\nSource revision 82a973c0 · Gradio 3.41.2 · Pillow 9.5.0\nAccessShared img2img upload; login only if configuredPathGradio image preprocessing converts pixels through PillowEvidenceImage input and preprocessing in pinned source\nAccessImage upload and preview on a reachable servicePathPreview opens and converts the uploaded file with PillowEvidenceUpload and preview routes in pinned source\nAccessImage upload with an account, or as a guest when enabledPathImage optimization calls Pillow thumbnail processingEvidenceUpload handler and optimization code in pinned source\nSource revision e87199c7 · image upload integration\nAccessAccount image upload; public thumbnail endpointPathThumbnail loads and resizes the image through PillowEvidenceUpload and thumbnail routes in pinned source\nAccessTask-data upload with an accountPathFrame worker calls Pillow Image.open().load()EvidenceTask route and frame worker in pinned source\nSource revision bcfdfcaa · official image includes Ghostscript\nAccessEmail attachment through a configured inboxPathPDF/A conversion calls Ghostscript directlyEvidenceMail importer and converter in pinned source\nAccessAuthenticated django-filer image uploadPathImage model opens the file with PillowEvidencePillow identification path in pinned source\nThe first ten entries record Upload2Shell execution. Gradio records a live HTTP-to-Ghostscript handoff; the remaining entries map application code to image-processing sinks.\nImage and document processing · Ghostscript 10.05.0\nAccessSigned-out request for an attacker-hosted fileObservedNative renderer control and a bounded worker file readFixedGoogle mitigated the affected path on 10 November 2026\nGhostscript 10.08.0 fixes Upload2Shell. Debian backported the upstream change into its security package. Ubuntu released fixed Ghostscript packages for seven supported releases on 21 October 2026; its notice described our font-loader finding before the CVE number was assigned. Application teams also closed routes into the renderer: WordPress fixed the Author+ upload path under CVE-2026-65640, and Roundcube restricted unsafe attachment image types before ImageMagick conversion under CVE-2026-114727. The technical writeup lists distribution package versions.\nWe found several other Ghostscript issues with lower or comparable impact and reported them upstream. Ghostscript sits beneath more file-processing features than most applications expose directly. We expect the security community to find additional software that reaches this vulnerability through uploads, thumbnails, print jobs, and document imports.",
