      "id": "theverge-2026-11-21-john-roberts-the-voice-of-linda-belcher-is-just-happy-to-fin",
      "title": "John Roberts, the voice of Linda Belcher, is just happy to finish a thing",
      "summary": "You probably know John Roberts best as the voice of Linda Belcher on Bob's Burgers. The show just wrapped up its 16th season and shows no signs of slowing down anytime soon. The show remains a reliable source of laughs, top-notch puns, and frankly wholesome fun.\nComedy is just part of Roberts' life, however. In addition to his appearances on Gravity Falls and Comedy Bang! Bang!, he's also a musici",
      "body": "You probably know John Roberts best as the voice of Linda Belcher on Bob’s Burgers. The show just wrapped up its 16th season and shows no signs of slowing down anytime soon. The show remains a reliable source of laughs, top-notch puns, and frankly wholesome fun.\nComedy is just part of Roberts’ life, however. In addition to his appearances on Gravity Falls and Comedy Bang! Bang!, he’s also a musician with deep roots in New York City’s queer nightlife scene. He just released his latest record, I Am, on Friday, and it dabbles in ’80s pop, ’90s house, and even dashes of ’00s rave. But while the record sounds made for the dance floor, it actually tackles some pretty heavy subject matter, like mortality, aging, and grief following the loss of his mother.\nDespite that, Roberts is still having fun, as you can see in the video for “Complicated,” which revels in the queer cult camp of Scorpio Rising, William Friedkin’s Cruising, and The Wolf Man.\nWhat is your most indispensable tool?\nWhich is the most underappreciated?\nWhat is the first app you install on a new phone or computer?\nWhat is one thing you wish you could change about your phone?\nWhat it does to my neck.\nWhich social media platform do you use the most?\nWhat is your happy place online?\nOld campy TV clips and music performances. Comedy.\nWhat is your favorite gadget you’ve ever owned?\nWhich was the most disappointing?\nAnything made after the year 2000.\nWhat game do you have the fondest memories of?\nWhich tech trend do you wish would go away?\nWhat is one thing you wish you had created?\n“Let’s Go Crazy” by Prince.\nWhat creation are you most proud of?\nWhich are you least proud of?\nWhat’s the best piece of advice you’ve ever received?\nWhat is your current obsession?\nWhat do you do when you need to focus?\nWhat do you do when you’re feeling stuck?\nWhen was the last time you went somewhere without your phone?\nWhat’s the last piece of physical media you bought?\nI got Madonna’s new album on Vinyl.\nWhat do you think is worth splurging on?\nWhat would the tagline for your biopic be?\nWhat’s the last GIF or meme you used?",
      "source": "The Verge",
