      "id": "bbc-2026-11-21-zelensky-says-crimean-bridge-strikes-fair-response-as-he-mee",
      "title": "Zelensky says Crimean Bridge strikes 'fair response' as he meets Wes Streeting",
      "summary": "Ukraine's president says Kyiv acted after 109 separate Russian aerial attacks on bridges in Ukraine.",
      "body": "Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky has justified Kyiv's repeated attacks on a critical bridge linking Russia to occupied Crimea, calling it a \"fair response\" to 109 separate Russian attacks on bridges in Ukraine.In comments to the BBC in Kyiv, Zelensky said the intense attacks on Ukraine by Russia that have followed the strikes on the Crimean Bridge were only a \"signal that Vladimir Putin does not want to stop. He wants a reason to escalate\".He rejected the claim by the Russian president that the bridge - which links Russia to the peninsula it illegally annexed from Ukraine - was \"exclusively civilian\" in use.\"There are facts, not just the words of Putin. We can see,\" he said.The Ukrainian president pointed to images online of tanks and other Russian military hardware using the route from Russia into occupied Crimea as a supply line and for logistics.\"If Putin used the internet, he could see that.\"The Ukrainian president added that Russia had carried out attacks with missiles and drones on bridges in Ukraine.This week's combined missile-and-drone strikes by Ukrainian forces destroyed the central road section of the Crimean Bridge, collapsing part of it together with one of the two support arches into the sea and rendering the structure unusable for road traffic.Russian attacks on Ukraine continued on Friday evening and overnight: a seven-year-old boy was killed in missile and drone strikes on Zelensky's hometown of Kryvyi Rih in the central Dnipropetrovsk region. Local officials say he had been in a playground at the time.A 20-year-old female medic was also killed. A local official added that when rescuers rushed to the scene, the same site was targeted again with jet powered drones. Another 58 people were injured in the city.Ukraine's state emergency service DSNS said 11 people were also injured in the north-eastern Kharkiv region, and one person in Rivne, in the north-west.Russia launched its full-scale invasion of Ukraine in February 2022.Zelensky was speaking ahead of a meeting in Kyiv with UK Defence Secretary Wes Streeting, who told the Ukrainian president he was here to show that Europe was united in its support.\"The more Putin tries to divide us, the more resolute we become,\" Streeting said.He said that Russian missiles hitting Poland on Friday, during military exercises of the so-called Coalition of the Willing, was an \"outrageous provocation\".The timing, Streeting said, seemed \"more than a coincidence\".Asked by the BBC about Nato's response, he said the best way was to \"do more for Ukraine\" to defend itself against Putin who he called a \"cold-blooded killer\".Streeting's description of Putin chimed with the comments made earlier by Zelensky, who described the Kremlin leader a \"killer\". This was done in response to US President Donald Trump referring this week to Putin as his \"friend\". Streeting's visit to Kyiv came after European leaders meeting in Berlin on Thursday alongside US envoys said they were ready for negotiations with Moscow on ending the war in Ukraine.\"Europe has a clear and consistent and united negotiating position,\" UK Prime Minister Andy Burnham said, while German Chancellor Friedrich Merz stressed that Moscow's \"maximalist demands are not realistic\".Donald Trump's son-in-law Jared Kushner, one of the two US envoys who were in Berlin, said the US president - who had also dialled into the meeting from Air Force One - wanted to make a deal with Moscow \"with Europe by his side\". Russia's Vladimir Putin has so far rejected any European role in the US-led peace talks - but earlier this week he invited European representatives to Moscow as it wanted to clarify \"what Europe will bring to these talks\".That meeting in the German capital came hours after Putin had held historic trilateral talks in Shenzhen, China, with Trump and Chinese President Xi Jinping.Zelensky said he had been \"sceptical\" ahead of the latest round of talks, when US envoys claimed that Russia was prepared to make compromises to end the war.\"I thought [Putin] would find reason to escalate.\"Speaking to the BBC, Streeting added: \"Putin has absolutely no business playing the victim. He is the aggressor in this war. He provoked an illegal invasion of Ukraine. And all of us, right throughout the world, need to judge Putin not on his words, but on his actions.\"",
      "source": "BBC",
      "category": "world",
      "tags": [],
      "author": null,
