      "id": "bbc-2026-11-21-money-box",
      "title": "Money Box",
      "summary": "The money stolen by criminals through fake investments doubles in just two years.",
      "body": "Home            News            Sport            Weather            iPlayer            Sounds            Bitesize     CBeebies     CBBC     Food         Home     News     Sport     Business     Technology     Health     Culture     Arts     Travel     Earth     Audio     Video     Live          Use BBC.com or the new BBC App to listen to BBC podcasts, Radio 4 and the World Service outside the UK.Find out how to listen to other BBC stationsEpisode detailsRadio 4,·21 Nov 2026,·28 minsNew Bank Services Law and Investment ScamsMoney BoxAvailable for over a yearThe government has set out a new law to force banks to make sure customers have access to face to face banking. The amendment to a Bill already going through Parliament came this week as a report was published warning that urgent action was needed to prevent \"further harm\" to people who need to go into a bank in person. This major review into access to banking was commissioned by the Treasury because of the continuing loss of branches from all the major banks. Paul Lewis interviews Richard Lloyd, who wrote this report.\nNew figures seen exclusively by Money Box show the amount of money taken in investment scams has doubled in just two years. In the first six months of this year UK Finance figures show more than one hundred million pounds was stolen from thousands of people, with experts saying the use of artificial intelligence is one of the reasons behind the rise.\nHeating your home will cost more in January - but seven different payments may help with those bills.  What are they and who's eligible?\nAnd, as we approach Black Friday, how to protect your money from fake offers and bargains.\nReporters: Dan Whitworth and Jo Krasner\nResearchers: Eimear Devlin and Jenni Lynam\nSenior News Editor: Sara Wadeson\n(First broadcast 12pm Saturday 21st November 2026)Programme WebsiteMore episodes",
