      "id": "hackernews-2026-11-21-adult-only-households-accounted-for-55-of-toy-sales-in-the-f",
      "title": "Adult-only households accounted for 55% of toy sales in the first half of 2026",
      "summary": "Article URL: https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2026-11-18/jellycats-squishmallows-and-lego-sets-for-adults-drive-holiday-traffic\nComments URL: https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50588436\nPoints: 37\n# Comments: 25",
      "body": "November 18, 2026 at 10:00 AM UTCUpdated on November 18, 2026 at 2:41 PM UTCTakeaways  by Bloomberg AIRachel Ellicott, 33, had just popped out to grab a coffee when the holiday window display at Nordstrom’s New York City flagship caught her eye. The upscale Midtown department store wasn’t spotlighting its usual luxury coats or designer handbags but an array of stuffed pickles, plush gargoyles and other children’s products — at adult prices.“I’ve never seen stuffed animals displayed in the window very prominently at a Nordstrom,” Ellicott said, darting into the store to check out the selection, including a small hot-chocolate plushie ($45) she said she’d sure like to add to the collection of Jellycats already scattered throughout her home. Although she generally spends more on gifts for her friends’ kids, Ellicott said she’ll often throw in a stuffie or two for herself as well. “They’re whimsical. They just make me happy.”",
