      "summary": "Article URL: https://www.backblaze.com/company/policy/privacy\nComments URL: https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50585593\nPoints: 47\n# Comments: 4",
      "body": "The Legal Basis for Processing Your Personal Information\nUnder the General Data Protection Regulation (“GDPR”) and/or the United Kingdom General Data Protection Regulation\n(“UK GDPR”), we are required to have a valid legal basis for processing your personal information, and we must\ninform you of that legal basis. Our legal basis for collecting and using the personal information described above\nwill depend on the specific personal information concerned and the context in which it is collected. Generally, we\nwill collect personal information from you only when you have consented to such collection, when we need the\npersonal information to perform our obligations under a contract with you (for example, when you create an account\nor use our services), or where the processing is in our legitimate business interests (for example, to detect and\nprevent fraud and to analyze usage for analytics, modeling, and business intelligence). In some cases, we may also\nhave a legal obligation to collect personal information from you (for example, to verify your identity when\naccessing your account or services).\nWhere we rely on legitimate interests, we balance our interests against your interests, rights, and freedoms and\napply appropriate safeguards to protect your personal data.\nIf we ask you to provide personal information to comply with a legal requirement or to enter into a contract with\nus, we will make this clear at the time we request that personal information. We will also tell you whether\nproviding that personal information is mandatory or not (as well as the possible consequences if you do not provide\nyour personal information). Similarly, if we collect and use your personal information, we will provide you with our\nlegitimate business interests for such collection and use.\nIf you have questions about or need further information concerning the legal basis for which we collect and use your\npersonal information, please contact us as provided in the\nContact for More Information section below.\nData Storage, Transfers, and Security\nWe use industry-standard methods of securing electronic databases of personal information. However, you should know\nthat no company can fully eliminate security risks associated with personal information. To help protect yourself,\nplease use a strong password, do not use the same password to access your Backblaze account that you use with other\naccounts or services, and protect your usernames and passwords to help prevent others from accessing your accounts\nYour personal information may be transferred to and processed in the United States and other countries where\nBackblaze and its service providers operate, which may have data protection laws that differ from those in your\nWhere required by law, we implement appropriate safeguards for such transfers, including contractual protections and\nother legally recognized mechanisms. While your information is outside of your country of residence, it is subject\nto the laws of the jurisdiction in which it is held and may be subject to disclosure to governments, courts, law\nenforcement, or regulatory agencies pursuant to applicable law.\nYour Data Protection and Privacy Rights and Choices\nIf you reside within the EEA or in the U.K., you have the following rights under applicable law, which you can\nRight of access: You can access your personal information that we collect.\nRight to rectification: You can correct, update, or delete your personal information and\nassociated data by logging into your account or contacting us as provided in the “Contact for More Information”\nRight to erasure: You can request deletion of your personal information, subject to certain\nRight to restrict processing: You can ask us to restrict the processing of your personal\ninformation where, for example, you contest the accuracy of the data or object to our processing.\nRight to data portability: Where applicable and technically possible, you can request that we\nprovide your personal information in a structured, commonly used, and machine-readable format.\nRight to object: You can object to the processing of your personal information where we rely on\nlegitimate interests as our legal basis.\nRight to withdraw consent: Where we have collected and processed your personal information with\nyour consent, you can withdraw your consent at any time. Withdrawing your consent will not affect the lawfulness\nof any processing we conducted prior to your withdrawal, nor will it affect the processing of your personal\ninformation conducted in reliance on lawful processing grounds other than consent.\nRight to opt out of marketing: You have the right to opt out of marketing communications we\nsend you at any time. You can exercise this right by using the unsubscribe link provided in each email. Please\nnote that even after you opt out, you will still receive service and transactional communications from us.\nRight to lodge a complaint: You have the right to complain to a data protection authority about\nour collection and use of your personal information. See the\nData Protection Authorities section below for\nPlease see the Exercising Your Privacy Rights section\nbelow to exercise your privacy rights.\nWe will respond to your request within 30 days of receipt. Where a request is complex, or we have received a large\nnumber of requests, we may extend this period by a further two months, as permitted under applicable law. If we\nextend the response period, we will inform you within 30 days of receiving your request and explain the reason for\nthe delay. We will not charge a fee for responding to your request unless the request is manifestly unfounded or\nexcessive, in which case we may charge a reasonable fee or decline to respond.\nIf you have an account, you may log in to access, update, or delete your personal information and associated data.\nIf you are unable to access your account, you may contact us using the information provided in the\nContact for More Information section below.\nObject or Restrict Data Processing\nIn cases where we rely on your consent to process personal information, you can revoke your consent by contacting\nus. Revoking your consent does not affect the lawfulness of any processing conducted prior to your withdrawal.\nYou may manage your cookie and tracking preferences through the cookie and tracking preference center, which may be\naccessed by clicking the Cookie Settings link in the footer of our website or\nthrough any other cookie settings mechanism made available on the Platform. Please note that cookie and tracking\npreferences are generally browser- and device-specific, and data collected before we can identify or authenticate\nyou may not be able to be associated with your account.\nBackblaze does not make decisions about you that produce legal effects or similarly significant effects based solely\non automated processing, including profiling. In particular, we do not use automated decision-making to make\ndecisions about your eligibility for services, pricing, or access to functionality. This does not prevent us from\nusing personal information for ordinary business purposes, such as analytics, lead management, marketing\nsegmentation, customer relationship management, fraud prevention, security, or service improvement, where such\nprocessing does not produce legal or similarly significant effects concerning you.\nIf you are not satisfied with how we handle your personal information, or with our response to a request you have\nmade, you have the right to lodge a complaint with the relevant data protection authority in your jurisdiction. You\nmay contact the applicable authority by clicking below:\nEuropean Economic Area (EU DPAs)\nUnited Kingdom (Information Commissioner’s Office)\nSwitzerland (Federal Data Protection and Information Commissioner)\nWe encourage you to contact us first using the information in the\nContact for More Information section below, so that we\nmay address your concerns directly.\nPlease read our Cookie Notice to learn about our practices regarding cookies and\nYou may access or modify your cookie and tracking preferences at any time by clicking the\nCookie Settings link in the footer of our website. The exact choices available to\nyou may depend on your location and the laws that apply to you.\nCookies: Cookies are small data files stored on your device when you visit. Cookies allow us to recognize your\ndevice during subsequent visits and personalize your experience based on your preferences. They may also provide\ninformation to our service providers to help us improve website functionality and usability.\nThe Platform may use first-party and third-party cookies, as well as other tracking technologies, for advertising\nand analytics purposes. First-party cookies are set directly by Backblaze and are used to make the Platform function\nproperly, remember your preferences, and support our internal analytics. Third-party cookies are set by our partners\nand service providers, such as advertising networks and analytics providers, and may be used to track your activity\nacross different websites to deliver targeted advertising and measure performance.\nIf you consent to the use of cookies by clicking “Accept All Cookies” when you first visit the website, we will\ncollect certain information from you, including Internet Protocol (IP) addresses, browser types, operating systems,\npage requests, and average time spent on our website. This data helps us understand website activity, monitor\nperformance, and improve the user experience.\nYou can set your browser to notify you when cookies are received or to block certain types of cookies. However,\ndisabling cookies may limit your ability to access some features of the website. For additional details on how to\nopt out of the use of cookies, please review our Cookie Notice.\nAnalytics: We utilize tools like Google Analytics to collect data about website usage, including pages visited, time\nspent, search terms, and engagement metrics. This information helps us evaluate and enhance the user experience. For\nexample, to opt out of Google Analytics, you can use the Google Analytics Opt-Out Browser Add-On. For more\ninformation about how Google uses your data, please visit “How Google uses data when you use our partners' sites or\napps.” Please review our Cookie Notice for information on analytics tools used on the website.\nInterest-Based Advertising: We work with third parties, such as advertisers, advertising networks, and data\nexchanges, to deliver tailored content and advertising based on your online activity. These third parties may use\ntheir own tracking technologies, including cookies and pixel tags, to collect information about your interactions\nTo opt out of interest-based advertising through cookies or similar technologies on our website, click the\nCookie Settings link in the footer of our website and update your preferences in\nour cookie and tracking preference center. You may also use industry opt-out tools, such as Your Online Choices,\nmay no longer be tailored to your preferences based on online behavior. Cookie-based opt-outs are generally browser-\nand device-specific, so you may need to repeat the opt-out process if you use a different browser or device or clear",
