      "body": "Home            News            Sport            Weather            iPlayer            Sounds            Bitesize     CBeebies     CBBC     Food         Home     News     Sport     Business     Technology     Health     Culture     Arts     Travel     Earth     Audio     Video     Live             Home            News            Sport            Weather            iPlayer            Sounds            Bitesize     CBeebies     CBBC     Food        Home     News     Sport     Business     Technology     Health     Culture     Arts     Travel     Earth     Audio     Video     Live         Close menu\nChristmasA-ZTV GuideWatchlistHomeTech NowAmerica's Cup: How Sailing is EvolvingTech Now - America's Cup: How Sailing is EvolvingAlasdair Keane is in Naples exploring how tech is transforming the America's Cup race, as Yasmin Morgan-Griffiths visits the Swiss startup that wants to generate electricity using railway tracks. Duration25 minsFirst shown21 Nov 2026Available for 11 monthsAudio DescribedSign LanguageEpisodes EpisodesThis episodeAmerica's Cup: How Sailing is EvolvingLandslides: Can Tech Save Lives?Yasmin Morgan-Griffiths follows a team testing AI early warning systems for landslides.Wildfires: Fighting Hidden HotspotsShiona McCallum visits Cairngorms National Park to see tech monitor wildfire damage.Alasdair Keane heads to the Pokémon World Championships in San Francisco.Ammie Sekhon explores tech used to identify and remove counterfeit products online.Adrienne Murray follows NASA scientists in Iceland researching a rare total solar eclipse.Can New Tech Help Assisted Births?Shiona McCallum meets mums and hospital staff trialling a new assisted birth innovation.\nInside Gamescom: The Big RevealsLaura Cress has the highlights from Gamescom, the biggest gaming convention in the world. Rainforests: Can Tech Help to Protect Trees?New technologies measuring forests and exclusive access to a hacker rehab programme.Inside the Esports World CupHighlights from the Esports World Cup in Paris and how to build a gaming PC.WWE: The Tech Behind the ShowAmmie Sekhon goes behind the scenes of WWE to see the tech that supports the show.Race for the Ultimate SupercomputerAdrienne Murray has rare access to Microsoft's Quantum Lab in Denmark.Adrienne Murray meets the team using technology to preserve a historic warship in Sweden.World Cup: Game-Changing TechShiona McCallum visits Fifa HQ in Zurich to see new tech being used in the World Cup.Shiona McCallum meets a medical expert testing out the future of prosthetics.Adrienne Murray explores how new 3D imaging is supporting heart procedures.Deep Dive: Underwater TechAndrew Rogers explores new tech trials helping people stay underwater for longer.Art Mystery: Can AI Solve It? Harriet Bradshaw finds out how AI is being used to help solve an art history mystery. Blenheim Palace: Can Tech Help to Restore it?Shiona McCallum tours Blenheim Palace, exploring the tech aiding its restoration.Climate Science in the CourtroomHow research linking climate change and extreme weather events is being used in lawsuits.Inside the High-Tech Insect FarmAlasdair Keane visits the underground insect farm turning food waste into animal feed.MWC Barcelona: What's New In Phone Tech?Paul Carter checks out the newest phones, gadgets and trends from MWC Barcelona. Norway's Fjords: Can Tourism Go Green?Alasdair Keane climbs aboard an electric boat in Norway.Inside Europe’s Space RaceAdrienne Murray visits the Esrange Spaceport in the extreme north of Sweden.Winter Olympics: Can Tech Boost Performance?Alasdair Keane visits the Olympic training centre in Oslo.Future Farming in AustraliaNick Kwek meets innovators using tech for Australia's agricultural industry.From Las Vegas, the latest trends and innovations at CES 2026.Jacqui Wakefield joins singer KT Tunstall as she sees her musical avatar.Space Exploration: Can Robots Lead the Way?Nick Kwek visits the National Space Industry Hub in Sydney.Icebreaker Tech: Navigating the ArcticAdrienne Murray meets the engineers designing icebreaker ship technology for the Arctic.",
