    {
      "id": "bbc-2026-11-20-white-house-removes-cyber-security-chief-after-series-of-tec",
      "title": "White House removes cyber-security chief after series of tech outages",
      "summary": "He has been fired after losing the confidence of new White House chief of staff Stephen Miller, according to reports.",
      "body": "The top cyber-security official in the US government is leaving his post after a little over a year in the job.White House National Cyber Director Sean Cairncross was fired after losing the confidence of the White House chief of staff, Stephen Miller, according CBS, the BBC's US news partner. Asked about his removal on Friday, President Donald Trump said it was because he was not \"good enough\".His firing comes after a string of tech outages which hit banking, air traffic control and other sectors. US officials said the outages were not caused by cyberattacks but the blackouts had sparked scrutiny from members of Congress who demanded a clearer explanation of what went wrong.There has been no official confirmation of the removal of Cairncross but Secretary of State Marco Rubio posted on X, external to say Department of Defense chief information officer Kirsten Davies was the new national cyber director.The news, first reported by Axios, external, follows security concerns, including the ability of advanced AI models - mostly from US companies - to discover vulnerabilities which humans would not be able to find on their own.Earlier this week, Rubio said there was \"zero evidence\" the outages were connected, adding \"we are not under systemic attack\". But the fact that so many have happened in quick succession has left some people worried about the safety of the tech which is heavily relied on in all aspects of daily life.",
      "source": "BBC",
      "category": "tech",
      "tags": [],
      "author": null,
