      "id": "hackernews-2026-11-20-openssl-buffer-overflow-in-evp-encodeblock-cve-2026-121481-c",
      "title": "OpenSSL: Buffer overflow in EVP_EncodeBlock() (CVE-2026-121481, CVSS 9.8)",
      "summary": "Article URL: https://github.com/openssl/openssl/pull/33652\nComments URL: https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50569226\nPoints: 319\n# Comments: 259",
      "body": "This fixes the buffer overflow in `EVP_EncodeBlock()` (CVE-2026-121481)\nby returning `-1` for invalid inputs. It also provides a similar guard\nfor `EVP_DecodeBlock()`, and fixes the incorrect length check in the\n`base64encode()` function of `http_client.c`. Also updates the\ndocumentation and adds new tests.\nThe community needs to establish a consensus how to move forward with the issue or PR\nThis fixes the buffer overflow in `EVP_EncodeBlock()` (CVE-2026-121481)\nby calling `OPENSSL_assert()` for inputs that lead to undefined\nbehavior. The same fix is applied to `EVP_DecodeBlock()`, and the\nincorrect length check in `base64encode()` of `http_client.c`\nis fixed. Also updates the documentation and adds new tests to document\nthe existing behavior for zero-length inputs.\nThis fixes the buffer overflow in `EVP_EncodeBlock()` (CVE-2026-121481)\nby calling `OPENSSL_assert()` for inputs that lead to undefined\nbehavior. The same fix is applied to `EVP_DecodeBlock()`, and the\nincorrect length check in `base64encode()` of `http_client.c`\nis fixed. Also updates the documentation and adds new tests to document\nthe existing behavior for zero-length inputs.\nThis fixes the buffer overflow in `EVP_EncodeBlock()` (CVE-2026-121481)\nby calling `OPENSSL_assert()` for inputs that lead to undefined\nbehavior. The same fix is applied to `EVP_DecodeBlock()`, and the\nincorrect length check in `base64encode()` of `http_client.c`\nis fixed. Also updates the documentation and adds new tests to document\nthe existing behavior for zero-length inputs.\nOpenSSL 4.x AVX2 encoder (openssl/openssl#33652 area) vs scalar via the\npublic API, toggling OPENSSL_ia32cap_P[2] bit 5; decode round trip as\nsecond oracle. Mismatch raises SIGABRT (shim swallows abort()).\nVendor default 4.1.0, stale-tree guard, version in build stamp, asm\nlibcrypto variant, apps/include workaround for 4.1.0 Configure.\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nBackport of the guards in openssl/openssl#33652\n(head ad8169a9bb, not merged yet; advisory pending) to 3.6.5:\n- EVP_EncodeBlock(): stop on a negative length or one whose base64\nencoding does not fit in an int (dlen > (INT_MAX / 4) * 3), where the\noutput length overflowed; an empty input writes only the NUL.\n- EVP_DecodeBlock(): 0 for an empty input, -1 for a negative length.\n- http_client.c base64encode(): reject lengths whose encoding would not\nfit in an int, not only len > INT_MAX (reachable through a long\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
