      "id": "bbc-2026-11-19-more-support-for-households-reliant-on-heating-oil",
      "title": "More support for households reliant on heating oil",
      "summary": "North Northamptonshire Council is encouraging eligible residents to apply for more support.",
      "body": "Households using heating oil as their main energy source are being offered more financial support by North Northamptonshire Council.Residents can apply for a £250 voucher in emergency situations where low oil levels would put health, safety or basic living conditions at risk.Heating oil is not protected by the Ofgem energy price cap, which means those reliant on it feel price increases faster than those on mains gas or electricity.The Reform UK-led council encouraged residents to see if they were eligible for support online, external.Heating oil prices have been volatile since the conflict between the US and Iran began in March.The government announced a £53m support package in response to rising costs.Rural areas, including parts of North Northamptonshire, are among the most affected, the council said.Greg Wilcox, its executive member for communities and rural affairs, added: \"We know that times are hard for many households and we want to do all we can to support as many residents as possible.\"",
