      "id": "bbc-2026-11-19-discrimination-claims-by-mcdonald-s-workers-can-go-ahead-cou",
      "title": "Discrimination claims by McDonald's workers can go ahead, court says",
      "summary": "McDonald's has said that \"ensuring a safe, respectful and inclusive working environment across our restaurants and offices remains a fundamental priority\".",
      "body": "A former McDonald's worker who says a manager failed to protect her when she was being sexualised by customers, has called on the firm to \"change the way they treat younger employees\".Hope, who worked at a branch in the West Midlands in 2023, also told BBC News she saw older colleagues eyeing up 16- and 17-year-old workers, and talking about wanting to sleep with them when they turned 18.McDonald's said: \"Ensuring a safe, respectful and inclusive working environment across our restaurants and offices remains a fundamental priority.\"BBC correspondent Noor Nanji looks at the latest developments.Read more on this story here.",
