      "body": "Home            News            Sport            Weather            iPlayer            Sounds            Bitesize     CBeebies     CBBC     Food         Home     News     Sport     Business     Technology     Health     Culture     Arts     Travel     Earth     Audio     Video     Live          Use BBC.com or the new BBC App to listen to BBC podcasts, Radio 4 and the World Service outside the UK.Find out how to listen to other BBC stationsEpisode detailsWorld Service,·19 Nov 2026,·27 minsPower players: Is Anthropic IPO a defining moment for AI?Business DailyAvailable for over a yearDario Amodei runs Anthropic, the company behind the Claude chatbot. He says artificial intelligence could help cure cancer, while warning it could also threaten humanity. As Anthropic starts selling shares through an initial public offering in New York, how do you put a value on a business making such extraordinary promises? Rahul Tandon and Will Bain are joined by the BBC's North America technology correspondent Lily Jamali to examine one of the most influential power players in artificial intelligence.\n(Photo: CEO of Anthropic Dario Amodei, addresses the gathering at the AI Impact Summit, in New Delhi, India, 19 February, 2026. He has short dark hair, black rimmed glasses and is wearing a black jacket, white shirt and tie. He gestures with his hand as he speaks. Credit: Bhawika Chhabra/Reuters)\nProducer: Barbara George and Matt Lines\nEditor: Stephen RyanProgramme WebsiteMore episodes",
