      "id": "hackernews-2026-11-18-inside-deutsche-bank",
      "title": "Inside Deutsche Bank",
      "summary": "Article URL: https://www.inside-db.com/\nComments URL: https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50547620\nPoints: 741\n# Comments: 246",
      "body": "Inside Deutsche Bank:                                Risky Business\nA major global investigation revealing the inner workings of the financial giant. The leak of 15+ million files lays bare the bank's flawed culture, systemic blind spots and pursuit of profit over compliance.\nInside Deutsche Bank: Secrets, scandals and double standards\nMore than 15-million internal files from the world’s biggest bank leak show an institution battling to stay the course on financial controls.\nLeaked files show Deutsche Bank undermined its climate pledges\nThe 15 million leaked internal documents offer a rare glimpse of what happened to those promises when they collided with lucrative financial relationships at the heart of one of Europe’s largest banks.\nLos pagos a la industria del sexo virtual en Colombia que el Deutsche Bank no vigiló\nIn Colombia, the bank's own investigation found it may have been instrumental in facilitating money laundering, human trafficking, and exploitation, among other crimes.\nDeutsche Bank’s Illicit Route to Prince Mohammed bin Nayef\nDeutsche Bank secured an investment portfolio worth hundreds of millions of dollars linked to Saudi Prince Mohammed bin Nayef and helped establish offshore corporate structures to manage it.\nLeaked Files Show Deutsche Bank Protected Russian Profits Despite Warnings\n“As you know we have a large Russian Oligarchs client population,” an analyst wrote as the bank braced for sanctions against wealthy clients.\nRead on The New York Times\nStudentský účet Michala Fica banka zrušila pro podezření z praní peněz\nRaising money laundering red flags, analysts at the bank found that the Slovak PM's son was not paying anything out of his account and was receiving payments from two people closely connected to his father's politics.\nA decade of dark money: Deutsche Bank’s bet on problematic payments\nDeutsche Bank has been sanctioned for failing to flag suspicious transactions properly, and this investigation reveals that it has continued to operate on the edge.\nBankrolling attacks in Gaza: how a global bank armed Israel\nDocuments in the Inside Deutsche Bank leak reveal Deutsche Bank’s role in supplying weapons now used against civilians in Palestine.\nDeutsche Bank slammed SA regulators, then hailed them as ‘world-class’\nThe Joburg office first slated local inspectors before a R38m fine. Then, in the same breath, had to praise them to HQ\nOrbán-linked bank was a gateway for Russian money into Europe, files reveal\nOne of Hungary’s largest banks allegedly platformed a multi-billion-euro money-laundering scheme linked to a Russian oligarch. Deutsche Bank, which processed many of its payments, struggled to curb the wrongdoing.\nRead on Follow The Money\nDeutsche Bank armata. Anche Leonardo tra i suoi clienti\nThe Inside Deutsche Bank leak reveals the bank's closeness to the war industry, and how it financed arms supplies to \"high-risk\" or conflict-ridden countries, violating its own internal policies.\nTrump, Deutsche Bank and the Russian connection\nDeutsche Bank documents connect Trump-owned companies to laundromat schemes.\n“Picaretas não melhoram”, disse executivo do Deutsche Bank sobre André Esteves, do BTG\n\"Crooks don’t improve miraculously as they get older\", said Deutsche bank executive about André Esteves, owner of BTG Pactual, the largest investment bank in Latin America.\nHow global banks helped Jho Low escape justice\nMore than a decade after implicated in the world's largest kleptocracy case, Jho Low remains elusive. Among his enablers was Deutsche Bank, which facilitated at least 24 transactions totalling €172.98 million linked to Low.\n[인사이드 도이체방크]도이체방크 엡스타인 '의심 거래' 6억 달러…알려진 액수의 두 배 넘어\nDeutsche Bank leak shows suspicious Epstein payments that double previously known figure.\nDeutsche Bank’s Illicit Route to Prince Mohammed bin Nayef\nDeutsche Bank secured an investment portfolio worth hundreds of millions of dollars linked to Saudi Prince Mohammed bin Nayef and helped establish offshore corporate structures to manage it.\nDeutsche Bank hired a Qatari royal. Why?\nLeaked documents reveal how dealings with royal dynasty blurred traditional boundaries between investor, client and counterparty\nEl Deutsche Bank financió las operaciones de la lista negra de empresas españolas investigadas por corrupción\nDeutsche Bank financed blacklisted operations involving Spanish companies under investigation for corruption.",
      "source": "Hacker News",
      "category": "tech",
      "tags": [],
      "author": "gyre007",
      "publishedAt": "2026-11-18T15:38:33.000Z",
      "imageUrl": "https://www.inside-db.com/content/images/size/w1200/2026/09/_DSF9639.jpg",
      "originalUrl": "https://www.inside-db.com/",
      "readTimeMinutes": 3,
