      "id": "theverge-2026-11-18-grand-theft-auto-vi-has-arrived",
      "title": "Grand Theft Auto VI has arrived",
      "summary": "More than a decade after Grand Theft Auto V was first released, its sequel is finally launching. On November 19th, GTA VI will be available on both the PS5 and Xbox Series X / S, and it’s quite possibly the most anticipated video game launch of all time.\nPart of this has to do with the success of its predecessor, as GTA V sold more than 230 million copies over the last 13 years. Some of it has to ",
      "body": "More than a decade after Grand Theft Auto V was first released, its sequel is finally launching. On November 19th, GTA VI will be available on both the PS5 and Xbox Series X / S, and it’s quite possibly the most anticipated video game launch of all time.\nPart of this has to do with the success of its predecessor, as GTA V sold more than 230 million copies over the last 13 years. Some of it has to do with the sheer length of time between releases, a period that was plagued by leaks and a handful of delays that made the wait even harder for fans.\nBut GTA VI is now a real thing you can play, and you can also keep track of all of the important post-launch information right here. That includes our own review and interviews with the development team, as well as news on just how the game ends up resonating with players.",
      "source": "The Verge",
      "category": "tech",
      "tags": [
        "Entertainment",
        "Gaming"
      ],
      "author": "Andrew Webster",
      "publishedAt": "2026-11-18T11:06:16.000Z",
      "imageUrl": "https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2026/11/STKS540_GTA_VI_2_A.jpg?quality=90&strip=all&crop=0,9.9676601489831,100,80.064679702034",
      "originalUrl": "https://www.theverge.com/entertainment/1035847/grand-theft-auto-6-launch-review-news",
      "readTimeMinutes": 1,
      "language": "en"
    },
    {
      "id": "bbc-2026-11-18-joanna-page-says-male-actor-made-awful-and-inappropriate-com",
      "title": "Joanna Page says male actor made 'awful' and 'inappropriate' comments to her on set",
      "summary": "Page spoke of the comments during Tuesday's episode of I'm a Celebrity... Get Me Out Of Here!",
      "body": "Joanna Page has said she was subjected to \"really inappropriate\" and \"awful\" comments from a fellow actor while on set.The Swansea-born actress, 48, told campmates on ITV's I'm a Celebrity… Get Me Out of Here! that the unnamed male actor had whispered \"awful stuff\" in her ear before a scene.\"He just spent the whole time just sort of making up this song and chanting about what he was going to do to me, and nobody said anything,\" she told fellow campmate Mariella Frostrup.Page has previously described feeling forced to laugh off being groped while filming with a \"handsy\" TV presenter.Page spoke of the inappropriate comments during Tuesday's episode of the reality show, as fellow celebrities, broadcaster Frostrup and model Leomie Anderson, discussed navigating male-dominated work environments in their careers.Page said the actor had come up to her \"before you were going to do a take or something\".\"And it was just, like, really inappropriate, awful stuff.\"",
      "source": "BBC",
      "category": "world",
      "tags": [],
      "author": null,
      "publishedAt": "2026-11-18T11:00:05.000Z",
      "imageUrl": "https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/ace/branded_news/1200/cpsprodpb/ca06/live/582be290-e33c-11f1-99a1-253766e7ad8b.jpg",
      "originalUrl": "https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cqj3kelenm0do?at_medium=RSS&at_campaign=rss",
      "readTimeMinutes": 1,
      "language": "en"
