      "id": "bbc-2026-11-18-i-want-to-know-if-toxic-lagoon-fire-caused-my-husband-s-rare",
      "title": "I want to know if toxic lagoon fire caused my husband's rare deadly cancer",
      "summary": "Steve Williams died of lung cancer 14 years after falling in to a lagoon at a toxic waste dump fire.",
      "body": "The council said it took \"its responsibilities for protecting public health and the environment extremely seriously\" and had carried out \"extensive investigations over many years\" into the Llwyneinion lagoon.Wrexham council added that concerns about the health of firefighters who attended the fire were raised with their contaminated land officer twice.The first was in February 2004 by the fire officer in charge at Wrexham fire station and on another occasion by a fire officer, who was told to speak to the health authority.On the risk of another fire on the site, Wrexham council said that in 2006 advice was sought from the fire service about this, but they were told a number of \"specific circumstances\" would need to occur for this to happen.An emergency response plan has been drawn up, and it was revisited in 2017.North Wales Fire and Rescue Service said it was not in a position to comment on the fire in 1980.It added: \"We recognise the importance of understanding the potential long-term health impacts associated with firefighting. Approaches to occupational health, wellbeing and health monitoring continue to be developed nationally as evidence, research and understanding across the sector evolve.\"The Welsh government announced in its draft budget on Tuesday that it would commit £2m to \"kick-start a new approach to managing contaminated land\".\"We are developing a Wales-wide strategy to progressively restore post-industrial land,\" the government said in a statement.\"We also continue to press the UK government for funding to address the legacy of Wales's industrial past, including the remediation of contaminated land.\"",
