      "id": "bbc-2026-11-18-mp-urges-council-to-speed-up-heating-oil-payments",
      "title": "MP urges council to speed up heating oil payments",
      "summary": "About 23,000 households use heating oil in Northumberland and face increasing bills this winter.",
      "body": "An MP has urged a council to speed up the process of heating oil support payments as energy prices soar.About 23,000 Northumberland homes use oil systems as they are not connected to the mains gas supply. Labour's North Northumberland MP David Smith said a freedom of information request from 21 September showed just over a third of households who applied for help with heating oil costs had received funding from Northumberland County Council.However, the Conservative-led local authority said its latest figures showed significantly more applications had now been approved almost two months on.Energy prices have increased due to ongoing conflicts around the world. Unlike gas, oil prices are not protected by the Ofgem Energy Price Cap, and households have experienced huge increases in the cost of filling tanks.Smith said the freedom of information request showed there had been 328 applications for heating oil assistance, but only 112 had been approved with total payments amounting to £36,123. The council said its figures showed more than 160 applicants and 40 venues had been supported, and there was no backlog for residents seeking support with heating oil, according to the Local Democracy Reporting Service. \"Those not receiving support are applicants who have not been able to demonstrate their household is either vulnerable or struggling to afford heating oil due to a low income,\" a spokesperson said.The government provided £5m to the county council through its Crisis and Resilience fund in April, including almost £500,000 to support households struggling with the cost of heating oil.Bamburgh Conservative councillor Guy Renner-Thompson has a home which uses a heating oil system. He urged the government to bring in more financial support, saying the council fully expected to spend the entire £498,459 heating oil allocation. Follow BBC North East on X, external, Facebook, external, Nextdoor and Instagram, external and listen to Radio Newcastle on BBC Sounds.",
      "source": "BBC",
      "category": "business",
      "tags": [],
      "author": null,
      "publishedAt": "2026-11-18T08:48:26.000Z",
      "imageUrl": "https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/ace/branded_news/1200/cpsprodpb/d421/live/2dc9e9f0-4399-11f0-ab6c-0dce3e1729a7.jpg",
      "originalUrl": "https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cm792dqz4qvyo?at_medium=RSS&at_campaign=rss",
      "readTimeMinutes": 2,
      "language": "en"
