      "id": "hackernews-2026-11-17-archive-team-is-archiving-the-apple-support-community",
      "title": "Archive Team is archiving the Apple Support Community",
      "summary": "Article URL: https://wiki.archiveteam.org/index.php/Apple_Discussions\nComments URL: https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50539747\nPoints: 236\n# Comments: 91",
      "body": "This project is in progress!\nDownload and run your warrior\nThe infrastructure for our distributed projects is expensive, and maintained by volunteers. If you appreciate what we do, consider making a donation to help cover our costs.\nApple Discussions, also known as the Apple Support Community and Apple Tech Exchange, is Apple’s online forum where customers ask questions, share advice, and troubleshoot Apple products and services.\nThe shutdown was announced on 2026-11-10 where the service will be shut down on 2026-11-20.[1]\nThe Apple Support Community will permanently close on November 20, 2026. Starting today, the site will no longer accept new posts and is available in a read-only state.\nYou can continue to find trusted guidance and support on the official Apple Support site.\nWe want to thank the community members who have contributed their time and expertise to help others with their Apple products.\nList of all the language sites\nThis  article  is a stub.  You can help Archiveteam by expanding it.",
