    {
      "id": "bbc-2026-11-17-jensen-huang-says-he-would-be-honoured-to-return-as-nvidia-c",
      "title": "Jensen Huang says he would be 'honoured' to return as Nvidia CEO if board asked him",
      "summary": "Huang says he has had an \"outpouring\" of calls from investors and others calling for him to return.",
      "body": "Jensen Huang said he would be \"honoured\" to return as the boss of tech giant Nvidia if the board asked him to, in his first public comments since his shock resignation.\"I created problems for the Board that I deeply regret. I own my mistakes completely,\" Huang said on X, days after reports he had extramarital affairs, including with an alleged Chinese spy. He said he had an \"outpouring\" of calls from company employees, investors and others calling for him to return as CEO of Nvidia.But, as the BBC reported on Monday, Nvidia's board is not considering bringing him back to lead the company.The prospect of Huang returning at this point looks unlikely. The company's board is investigating his conduct, which includes an alleged affair with an Nvidia executive. The AI chip giant is set to report its financial results later on Tuesday, during which the company's interim chief executive, Collette Kress, may address the situation with Huang.Beyond the internal Nvidia investigation, Huang's affair with a woman suspected of being an asset for Beijing is set to see the billionaire questioned before multiple committees of US lawmakers in the weeks ahead.The Nvidia founder said he had \"made serious mistakes in my personal life\".Nonetheless, Huang's statement appeared to show some hope he would be able to move past the major corporate scandal. Huang said people have continued to \"reach out to me directly as the company navigates complex technology, market, competitive, and geopolitical dynamics\".\"If the board of directors decides that my return is in the best interest of our shareholders, our employees, the company, and America, I would be honoured to answer these calls and return as CEO,\" Huang added.Many technology executives in recent days have praised Huang's role in the artificial intelligence boom. A petition began circulating online over the weekend calling for his reinstatement at the company.Yet, by Monday, many executives were not openly calling for Huang's return.Brad Gerstner, a major tech investor who knows Huang personally and also holds a significant stake in Nvidia, last week wrote an open letter saying that Nvidia could consider Huang's reinstatement. On Monday, Gerstner said during an event hosted by Semafor that his letter had been misunderstood and the investigation into Huang's conduct needed to run its course.While Gerstner questioned the facts around Huang's departure, he added: \"I don't know to what degree he misled the board. If I was on a board I would take that very seriously. Let's be clear no one is above the law.\"",
      "source": "BBC",
      "category": "business",
