      "id": "bbc-2026-11-17-woods-set-to-return-next-month-after-two-years-out",
      "title": "Woods set to return next month after two years out",
      "summary": "Tiger Woods is set to return to competitive golf in December for the first time in more than two years.",
      "body": "Tiger Woods is set to return to competitive golf in December for the first time in more than two years.Woods, 50, has not played in a traditional ranking event since the 2024 Open Championship at Royal Troon amid a series of off-course issues.The 15-time major champion has endured a challenging few years with a number of injuries and turmoil in his personal life.Woods will host next month's Hero World Challenge - an event which is part of the PGA Tour schedule but does not carry FedEx Cup points - and has been announced as part of the 20-player field.The American is one of three exemptions for the tournament in the Bahamas along with compatriots Rickie Fowler and Gary Woodland.Speaking to SiriusXM PGA Tour Radio in a video posted last week, Woods said: \"I'm feeling better, no doubt about that.\"I've been training quite a bit. I will be at Hero either way, so I'll see you there.\"Woods' long-awaited return comes after he accepted a five-year driving ban in September following a plea agreement in his reckless driving case.In March, Woods had been arrested and charged with driving under the influence after clipping a truck and rolling his car in Florida.Woods was also found with two white pills in his pocket, which were identified as hydrocodone - an opioid used to treat pain.He subsequently stepped away from golf to seek treatment in what was described by his attorney as an \"intensive, highly individualised and medically integrated programme\".Woods has endured a succession of debilitating injuries, including multiple back surgeries, serious fractures to his right leg following a car crash in 2021 and a ruptured Achilles tendon in 2025.Woods also suffered the death of his mother, Kultida, in February 2025, while his girlfriend Vanessa Trump was diagnosed with breast cancer earlier this year.Trump, the former daughter-in-law of US President Donald Trump, said last month that she is now cancer free.Every report we had since Tiger Woods resurfaced into public life has told us he is looking good and looking fit. Going into the new year he will be taking part in his own indoor golf league, the TGL, so it's not the biggest surprise that he will be at his own tournament in the Bahamas.This is the fifth time he has come back from a long-term absence from the game at this event. It is one that means an awful lot to him. It is involved with his charitable foundation and it's his tournament, so no surprise this is the one he has chosen to come back at.The TGL in the new year, that's the indoor simulator run by his company in conjunction with Rory McIlroy. He did compete last year and cut a pretty pathetic figure by the standards of someone who has won 15 major titles. We could see him play before that at the PNC event. That's the parent and child event where he would presumably play with his son Charlie.He is trying to line himself up to play at least the majors next year. They mean an awful lot to him.We know how much the Masters means to him, but also think about where the US Open is going to be played, at Pebble Beach, and that's where he won the US Open in 2000 by 15 shots.The Open Championship at St Andrews where he has won two of his three Open titles. These would be events he would certainly want to be at.",
      "source": "BBC",
      "category": "world",
