      "id": "techcrunch-2026-11-17-nvidia-s-first-big-move-after-jensen-huang-s-exit-targets-na",
      "title": "Nvidia’s first big move after Jensen Huang’s exit targets national security",
      "summary": "The new standing committee will give board-level oversight of national security policies, export control compliance, and global trade risks, the company said.",
      "body": "6:05 AM PST · November 17, 2026\nImage Credits:David Paul Morris/Bloomberg / Getty Images\nNvidia has formed a committee to oversee national security policies and export control compliance following the abrupt resignation of CEO Jensen Huang over allegations of an affair with a suspected Chinese spy who had links to one of the company’s customers.\nNvidia said Tuesday that the new standing committee will give board-level oversight of national security policies, export control compliance, and global trade risks. The move comes amid increased scrutiny from U.S. lawmakers over Huang’s alleged ties to the suspected spy and his advocacy for easing restrictions on advanced AI chip exports to China.\nThe Commerce Department said Monday it was planning to introduce new export controls on AI chips and data centers outside of the U.S. in an effort to prevent companies in China and elsewhere from circumventing existing rules by remotely accessing AI infrastructure located in other countries. The interim rule was made in direct response to the unfolding chip smuggling scandal at Nvidia.\nThe announcement comes just a few hours before Nvidia’s highly anticipated third-quarter earnings call. Analysts, the media, and shareholders expect the company to address the controversy and outline how it might affect operations. This is the first major action by the company under the leadership of Collette Kress, the company’s CFO who took over as interim CEO after Huang stepped down last week.\nThe committee, which will meet at least quarterly, will be chaired by director Suzanne Nora Johnson and include fellow directors Stephen C. Neal and John O. Dabiri as members.\nNvidia already has a national security team and global trade compliance team. Those teams will now report to this board committee and Kress on day-to-day operations.\nHuang has agreed to testify before Congress later this month.\nSubscribe for the industry’s biggest tech news",
      "source": "TechCrunch",
      "category": "tech",
      "tags": [],
      "author": "Kirsten Korosec",
      "publishedAt": "2026-11-17T14:05:30.000Z",
      "imageUrl": "https://techcrunch.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/10/GettyImages-2087335475.jpg?resize=1200,799",
      "originalUrl": "https://techcrunch.com/2026/11/17/nvidias-first-big-move-after-jensen-huangs-exit-targets-national-security/",
      "readTimeMinutes": 2,
      "language": "en"
    },
