      "id": "bbc-2026-11-17-met-office-yellow-warning-in-place-as-snow-could-disrupt-tue",
      "title": "Met Office yellow warning in place as snow could disrupt Tuesday morning travel",
      "summary": "Snow could bring some transport disruption to the hills of northern England and southern Scotland, as Chris Fawkes explains.",
      "body": "A weather front is pushing north and east across the UK bringing a spell of rain to many areas. As this rain reaches northern England it will encounter a reservoir of colder and drier air. Some of the rain will evaporate in this drier air, which will cool the atmosphere further by a process known as evaporative cooling - the same process involved in cooling your body down when you sweat. Eventually rain will start to turn to snow, initially over higher hills in the Pennines, moving to lower hills with time. As the precipitation moves northwards and eastwards, the snow will spread to the Cumbrian hills and into Scotland's Southern Uplands.The snow will come down in big, wet, chunky flakes which could stick to powerlines and tree branches. The extra weight of the snow combined with wind gusts of 40-50mph over high ground could bring down tree branches and powerlines, bringing an additional risk of some localised power cuts.",
      "source": "BBC",
      "category": "world",
      "tags": [],
      "author": null,
      "publishedAt": "2026-11-17T00:09:54.000Z",
