      "id": "theverge-2026-11-15-the-sony-aibo-was-a-robot-revolution-dressed-like-a-dog",
      "title": "The Sony Aibo was a robot revolution dressed like a dog",
      "summary": "In the 1990s, Sony was absolutely convinced that we were on the precipice of a robot takeover. Pretty soon, the company decided, we'd all be living among countless humanoid robots. Some would be our coworkers; others would be our friends; and at least one would be our pet. And \"pet\" was exactly what Sony was going for when it created the Aibo. It was supposed to be part of the family.\nOn this epis",
      "body": "In the 1990s, Sony was absolutely convinced that we were on the precipice of a robot takeover. Pretty soon, the company decided, we’d all be living among countless humanoid robots. Some would be our coworkers; others would be our friends; and at least one would be our pet. And “pet” was exactly what Sony was going for when it created the Aibo. It was supposed to be part of the family.\nOn this episode of Version History, we go back in time and tell the story of the Aibo. David Pierce is joined by The Verge’s Victoria Song and Jennifer Pattison Tuohy, and together they discuss the origins of this remarkable robot dog, and its impressive success and longevity. They also try to figure out why Aibo had such an effect on its owners, what Sony got right (and wrong) about robots, and whether the idea of a robo-pet will ever be a global phenomenon.\nThis is the first episode of the sixth season of Version History. We’re back! This season is all about pets: gadgets that are pets, gadgets for your pets, and one gadget called pet. We’ll be in your feeds for the next six weeks — if you want to be sure not to miss anything, there are a few ways to subscribe:\n* The Version History podcast feed\n* The Version History YouTube channel\n* Our TikTok and Instagram accounts\nIf you’re a Verge subscriber, you can also get access to Version History (and all our other podcasts) with no ads. All you have to do is visit your account settings.\nIf you want to know more about the Aibo, here are some links to get you started:\n* From The New York Times: A Smart Dog With Megabytes\n* From Businessweek: This Cute Little Pet Is A Robot\n* From IEEE Spectrum: QRIO: The Robot That Could\n* The Robots Guide guide to Aibo\n* From The Wall Street Journal: In Japan, Dog Owners Feel Abandoned as Sony Stops Supporting ‘Aibo’\n* The Aibo in the Museum of Modern Art\n* I played with Sony’s new Aibo robot dog, and I miss it already",
      "source": "The Verge",
      "category": "tech",
      "tags": [
        "Podcasts",
        "Robot",
        "Tech",
        "Version History"
      ],
