      "id": "hackernews-2026-11-13-show-hn-live-map-of-u-s-flights-during-tonight-s-faa-nationw",
      "title": "Show HN: Live map of U.S. flights during tonight's FAA nationwide ground stop",
      "summary": "Article URL: https://grounds.top/\nComments URL: https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50491545\nPoints: 160\n# Comments: 22",
      "body": "grounds.top: FAA nationwide ground stop, Nov 13, 2026\n—airline flights in the airin the air\n—of normal departuresof normal departures\n—departures missed since 3:30 pmdepartures missed\nOn Nov 13, 2026 the FAA ordered a ground stop at every U.S. airport at 3:54 PM ET. This page shows tracked flights over the U.S., live and replayable, against the same time a week earlier.\nAirport departures, last 30 min vs a week earlier:\nMissing from the sky—flights that were airborne at this time last Friday\nDepartures missed since 3:30 pm (est.)——\nFlight positions: adsb.fi community ADS-B network. Airport delay feed: FAA NAS Status. An independent, unofficial page, not affiliated with the FAA. Hover or tap a dot to identify the aircraft.\nEstimated commercial departures missed since 3:30 pm ET: the count for the same hours a week earlier minus this week's, from tracking data. On the right, how many left, out of the number a week earlier. Dot: departures in the last 30 minutes (red almost none, amber reduced, green near normal).\nAircraft in the air at the selected time. The bar is the share of the same time a week earlier.\nCarrierAirborneShare of a week earlierSince 1 pm\n—. The feed lists only airports with a specific entry; during the nationwide stop every US airport is affected, listed or not.\nFrom news reports; updated by hand, not live.",
      "source": "Hacker News",
